Description:  Alchemists are wizards who specialize in the making and
usage of potions.

Class intrinsics:

Bonuses to intelligence.
Penalties to strength (which is why he's in a brainy field to start
with) .
Bonus to dexterity (you don't last long as a clumsy alchemist).
Penalty to wisdom (People who have wisdom don't get into fields
involving mixing nasty chemicals).
Penalty to Charisma (hard to be charismatic when you don't have any
eyebrows).

Class abilities:
Able to identify any potion on sight.
level 1:  poison resistance (can't imagine why an alchemist would need
this).
level 10: shock resistance (being blown up too many times has given you
a resistance to shocks).

When performing alchemy between two "other" potions,  bonus to chances
of getting a helpful result, as opposed to sickness or suchlike.

New tool: Alchemist's kit.

When applied against a potion of water by an alchemist,  prompt to ask
what kind of potion to make.  Roll against experience level and
intelligence. If successful, change potion of water into one potion of
ANY type.  Higher level potions (such as gain level) require a higher
roll than low-level potions such as healing.    Failed roll results in
potion from "other vs. other" alchemy table.

Alchemist's kit has a limited number of charges (say, 12).

If used by non-alchemist, or cursed, produces random potion instead of
desired potion, from alchemy table of "other vs. other" potion mixing.



Quest Leader: Sir Isaac Newton (who was a noted alchemist as well as
physicist)
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Newton%27s_occult_studies

Quest Artifact:  Philosopher's Stone.
Carried: Magic resistance. half damage (spell or physical, haven't
decided).
Invoked:  Produces 1 potion of whatever type you choose, from nothing,
no possibility of failure, every time.

Quest Nemesis:  Unknown. Can't think of a really iconic villain who was
an  alchemist right now. Should be an archlich (it requires a potion to
make one, after all, and one of those would certainly be a grasping
megalomaniac).  Should also be modified using alchemy (unusual
strength, HP), possess multiple potions (for throwing and for drinking)
and be guarded  monsters associated with alchemy (golems, zombies).

Quest Lair: Alchemy lab. Lots of creepy equipment, multiple potions.

